  (wire (pts (xy 635.00 139.70) (xy 635.00 142.24)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid 3c31f201-1f7e-4412-9538-e197dafb4a9b))
  (label "PV+" (at 635.00 142.24 270) (fields_autoplaced)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid 4289f022-4f79-4cee-8da8-ab42f868ac57))
  (text "Current paths" (at 615.00 170.00 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 15ed2f54-f805-447b-b584-a3a732c9ee3a))
  (text "1. SUN-SENSOR LOOP: J1 -> D0 -> Q1 -> RSH1 -> GND\n   Panel short-circuit current, ~1 ms every 10 s. Panel Isc 5.40 A (label), max ~6 A in cold strong sun.\n   A vertical panel peaks near 1.8 A at noon. The panel cannot supply more than its Isc.\n2. BOARD SUPPLY: PV+ -> F1 (2 A) -> D1 (3 A) -> buck -> +5V\n   Under 0.3 A continuous. F1 and D1 are NOT in the measured current path:\n   F1 sits after the Q1 node so the short-circuit pulses never pass through it.\n3. AUX (optional add-on): PV+ -> F4 (fitted only with an add-on; <= 3 A on v1, 9 A only with D5 on a heatsink) -> D5 -> J12\n   Never through the shunt. D0 and D5 need cooling above ~2 A.\nJ1 and J12 '>= 15 A' is the terminal and wire rating, not a measured current." (at 615.00 176.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 9144a88b-6630-4369-917d-e99219aaf72c))
  (text "Measurement ranges" (at 615.00 225.00 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 3d9dbf52-7767-4adf-9115-c08e29d37837))
  (text "ISENSE (GPIO 35): RSH1 5 mOhm x INA180A3 gain 100 = 0.5 V/A.\n   Measured range 0-6 A (pulsed). 1.8 A -> 0.9 V; 5.4 A -> 2.7 V. Output clamps at the 3.3 V supply (~6.6 A): harmless.\n   Gain 100 is deliberate: low vertical-panel currents stay well inside the ADC's range.\n   Shunt dissipation 0.18 W only during each 1 ms pulse; 2 W rating is for pulse robustness.\nVDIV (GPIO 34): R1 100k / R2 4k7 = x 22.3 (R2 was 5k6, changed after review).\n   Panel Voc 44.5 V -> 2.00 V; cold morning 48 V -> 2.15 V; board rating 60 V -> 2.69 V.\n   ESP32 ADC accurate to ~2.45 V (= 54 V panel); pin absolute max 3.6 V. R1 limits any fault current to < 1 mA.\n   Firmware: DIVIDER = (100 + 4.7) / 4.7 (pva-fw-6.1.1)." (at 615.00 231.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid 97d83c21-451d-4a9b-92f1-8b4ec6191ff2))
  (text "ESP32 module and Q1 gate (review 2)" (at 615.00 285.00 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 04827519-a035-4b08-b6f1-5512c84a8033))
  (text "The ESP32 is a complete ELEGOO dev board plugged into J14/J15. Its EN pull-up, reset and boot buttons,\nUSB-serial converter and strapping resistors are on that board, not on the carrier.\nEN and GPIO 0, 1, 2, 3, 12, 15 are deliberately not brought out. GPIO 5 (strapping) is held high by R14.\nQ1 gate: U3 drives it when +5V exists; R21 (100k, gate-source) holds Q1 off before that, at dawn.\nD6 (TVS on PV+): footprint only; fitted if the v1 bench test shows turn-off overshoot. Then Q1 >= 100 V." (at 615.00 291.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid afb5a633-cbed-4610-b7f7-167f92a574a8))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
